<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Puebla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5 May 1862</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-french-intervention-in-mexico">Second French intervention in Mexico</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Puebla was fought on 5 May 1862 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-french-intervention-in-mexico">French intervention in Mexico</a>, when Mexican troops under General Ignacio <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a> repulsed a French assault on the forts above Puebla. Although the French took Puebla the following year, the victory became a national symbol of resistance. It is commemorated as Cinco de Mayo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-puebla.jpg" alt="Battle of Puebla" width="320" height="258" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batalla_de_Puebla,_5-5-1862_(1870).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
